  "title": "Erdős Problem #611",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For a graph $G$ let $\\tau(G)$ denote the minimal number of vertices that include at least one from each maximal clique of $G$ (sometimes called the clique transversal number).\nIs it true that if all maximal cliques in $G$ have at least $cn$ vertices then $\\tau(G)=o_c(n)$?\nSimilarly, estimate for $c>0$ the minimal $k_c(n)$ such that if every maximal clique in $G$ has at least $k_c(n)$ vertices then $\\tau(G)<(1-c)n$.",
